From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: notepad: a real editor -- tabs, syntax colours, exact encodings

Wine's Notepad is the system EDIT control in a window: it rewrites every
line end to CRLF, cannot save UTF-16 BE or keep a UTF-8 BOM choice, has one
level of undo, no tabs, no highlighting, and crawls on large files. This
replaces programs/notepad with an editor of the Kate / Notepad++ class that is
still notepad.exe -- system32 and syswow64 -- for every program, script and
file association that runs it.

Our own editor control (editor.c), not Scintilla: a gap buffer of UTF-16 text
with a line index (textbuf.c) that keeps line ends exactly as the file had
them (CRLF, LF, CR, even mixed), so an unchanged document saves the same
bytes; only the lines on screen are laid out and coloured. Character advances
come from a per-font cache and are handed to ExtTextOutW, so caret and pixels
always agree; glyphs the font lacks come from installed fallback fonts.
Multi-level undo/redo grouped by word, word wrap, zoom, line numbers, current
line, matching brackets, whitespace, auto-indent, tabs or spaces, line
operations, comment toggling, and the EDIT messages (WM_GETTEXT, EM_GETSEL,
EM_REPLACESEL, ...) for programs that drive Notepad's text.

 - fileio.c: BOM, UTF-16 without BOM, valid UTF-8, else ANSI; save in any of
   UTF-8, UTF-8 with BOM, UTF-16 LE/BE, ANSI (with the loss warning).
 - syntax.c: C/C++, C#, Java, Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, JSON, XML,
   HTML, CSS, INI, .reg, PowerShell, batch, shell, Markdown, SQL, YAML, Rust,
   Go -- a line at a time from the state the line before ended in.
 - regex.c: find/replace with regular expressions (groups, back-references,
   lazy quantifiers), a backtracking machine with an explicit stack and a step
   budget, so no pattern can overflow the stack or hang the editor.
 - main.c: tabs (Ctrl+N/T, Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Tab, drag to reorder, middle-click),
   a find/replace bar (match case, whole word, regex, "n of m", find as you
   type), a status bar (Ln/Col, zoom, line ends, encoding, language -- each
   clickable), recent files, reload when changed on disk, reopen the last
   session's files, Save As with encoding and line-end choices, printing with
   header/footer, drag and drop, light and dark themes in the Stained Glass
   purple.

Windows compatibility is kept deliberately: one process per invocation that
lives until its window closes (git's core.editor, start /wait), the command
line (/p, /pt, /a, /w, unquoted paths with spaces, ".txt" tried, "create
it?"), the "Notepad" window class and "<name> - Notepad" title, settings in
HKCU\Software\Microsoft\Notepad, and .LOG time stamps.

Why not Scintilla/Lexilla: it would be a C++ dependency fetched and built
inside Wine's PE build, and the project prefers owning a clean-room
implementation; what Notepad needs is a few thousand lines of C that the
rest of this series can maintain. No Microsoft code or artwork; the icon is
Wine's.

The menu bar follows the theme too: in the dark theme Notepad draws the
bar's items itself (owner-drawn, with their Alt keys) on a dark bar, which
win32u paints with the menu's MIM_BACKGROUND brush (0188). Page Setup has
Windows Notepad's Header and Footer boxes (a hook grows the common dialog);
they are kept as szHeader/szTrailer, and &l, &c, &r place what follows them
left, centred or right (with &f, &p, &d, &t, &&). NOTEPAD_PRINT_EMF=<dir>
prints each page as an EMF there, for tests.

A minimap (View > Minimap; by default for code files, not plain text): a
strip right of the text with the whole document in miniature, coloured by
the highlighter, the lines on screen shaded; a click centres the editor on
the line under it, dragging follows. A long document is compressed to the
strip's height (a pixel row per n/h lines) and only the rows shown are
drawn, lexing no further than the editor already has, so a 300 000-line
file costs no more than its view.

Gates: test/notepad-gate.sh (make test-notepad),
test/notepad-print-gate.sh (make test-notepad-print) and
test/notepad-minimap-gate.sh (make test-notepad-minimap).
